<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span><span id="S4.T3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation Studies of Loss Functions in Domain Disentangling Loss (DDL).</span>
DDL employs two loss functions: Cross-Entropy (CE) and Maximum Mean Discrepancy (MMD).
Using both losses together yields the best-balanced trade-off, as shown by <math id="S4.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>.
</figcaption>
