<figure id="A2.T13" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 13: </span><span id="A2.T13.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation Study of Loss functions.</span>
We evaluate the individual and combined impact of <math id="A2.T13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{memorize}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>memorize</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{memorize}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.T13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{forget}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>forget</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{forget}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.T13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{domain}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>domain</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{domain}}</annotation></semantics></math> on memorization (<span id="A2.T13.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Mem</span>), forgetting (<span id="A2.T13.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For</span>), and the overall balance metric <math id="A2.T13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>.
The results show that each loss function contributes to different aspects of performance, and their combination achieves the best trade-off.
</figcaption>
