</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A5.F7.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.08132v1/img_dir/imagenet_promptdepth.png" id="A5.F7.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:179/107;" width="179" height="107" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F7.sf3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(c)</span> </span><span id="A5.F7.sf3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">ImageNet</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="A5.F7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Sensitivity to Propmt Depth.<span id="A5.F7.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We report the performance when varying the depth at which the InstaPG is inserted.
The standard vision prompt is also applied up to the same layer.
The stable results across depths demonstrate the robustness of our method to the choice of insertion point.
</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A5.T15" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A5.T15.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 15</span>: </span><span id="A5.T15.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Performance with SigLIP on ImageNet.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A5.T15.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
